          <baseCommit>49fec179d6e7f8fc89c4e8ee6c721cd661e9db20</baseCommit>
          <output>Task complete. Summary of what `A03_01_CopyData.run()` did:

1. Deleted the live `a03_authoring/data` tree and copied the full `a02_structuring/data` tree in its place (45 files, matching A02's count).
2. Renamed `BmlDocSet_A02.bml` → `BmlDocSet_A03.bml` and remapped every A02→A03 package/name reference (xmlns URIs, FQN comments, element names, prose) across all 45 files.
3. Fixed the two spots blind substitution would've gotten wrong: `BmlDocSet_A03`'s documentation (which named nonexistent tasks `A03_02_UpdatePageSkeletons`/`A03_03_UpdatePageGroups`) now correctly says pages/pageGroups/homePage/rootPageGroup are filled by `A03_01_CopyData` and content is authored by `A03_02_AuthorPages`; `TableOfContents.bml`'s prose was reworded to a self-referential form instead of naming another sector.
4. `npx blockml validate` shows zero errors/warnings introduced in `a03_authoring/data` (only pre-existing style recommendations, same as A02's originals).
5. `org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library` catalog already exported every A03 data Block from the prior run, so no export changes were needed.

Net effect: the diff is 35 files with only deletions — the previously authored `&lt;content>` page bodies from the last `A03_02_AuthorPages` run are gone, which is correct: this task wipes and rebuilds A03 skeletons fresh from A02 every run, and content is re-authored by the next operation in the transformation. Per the `ExecuteTask` contract, I made no changes under `_meta/transform/` and did not commit — the operation envelope owns that.</output>
